From: j7 g3d
Subject: j7prime: Mali-T830 user client (j7gpu=7) and a kernel-side client selftest

j7gpu=6 passed on the phone. Layer on top: the kernel interface an app-side GL driver needs.
With j7gpu=7 the driver keeps the GPU reset+powered, AS0 programmed and the page-table pool
alive, and registers the user-client class J7MaliUserClient (property kIOUserClientClassKey)
on the GPU service. Selectors: 0 map client memory (kernel wires it and maps it into AS0 at a
kernel-chosen VA), 1 unmap, 2 submit a job chain (VA must lie in a mapping the client owns),
3 wait (status 0 / -1 timeout / -2 job fault / -3 MMU fault, then GPU reset + repower +
AS0 reprogram so the next call works), 4 info, 5 log a string into the kernel log (so a
user-space test can report through the persistent log). Cache clean/flush around submit/wait is
done by the kernel over all maps for now; AS0 is shared by all clients.

Because no user-space binary can be put on the phone cheaply, j7gpu=7 also runs a
kernel-side client at boot: it creates a J7MaliUserClient with kernel_task as the owning task
and drives the real externalMethod() entry points: info, log, map, good job chain, a
deliberate fault (checks the recovery), good chain again, a submit for an unowned VA (must be
refused), unmap.

Host-tested against a simulated Mali with incoherent caches (same code passes; with cache
maintenance disabled the test fails). The IOUserClient plumbing mirrors the Pixel repo's
proven SweetGPUUserClient but has NOT been compiled against this xnu: if the xnu build fails
after adding this patch, drop 0311 and 0304-0310 still build.

